  "details": "I suggest to count area of textures used in avatars.\nThat's because some players use unnecesary huge textures (especially when there is also too many unatlased materials). Before I met players used few 8k textures which is absurdly unnecesary. With my experience for most avatars 4k altas (16M pixels) are more than enough. And for some specific avatars with flat colored clothes and skin w/o details, 2k atlas (4M pixels) is also fine. Reducing textures area can save video memory usage. If a lot of players with huge tex avatars joins instance of world with also detailed textures, average graphic card can run out of memory causing performance problems. \n\nThis also can motivate creators to use atlasing, as some unused parts of textures will not be included into build. (Especially MMD-based avatars where, for example, 2k full-cloth texture used just to pick some small acessory like hairpin from other MMD model.)",
